{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Is it for HaShem that you requite this?</b> He used the language of גמול (requital) to admonish that in place of their requiting Him with goodness for all that He requited them with goodness, behold, they repay evil for good." "<b>A base nation and not wise.</b> And 'wise' is not the opposite of 'base' — to say that even if they are a base nation by nature, if they were wise they would not be base toward HaShem, for the base man recognizes that withholding from uprightness stems only from want, and he would not be base." "<b>And this</b> is what the verse concluded: ״הֲלוֹא הוּא אָבִיךָ״ and so on. He arranged four categories: First, that He created man, and corresponding to this He said ״הוּא אָבִיךָ״. Second, that He acquired us as servants by bringing us out of Pharaoh's hand and sustaining us in the wilderness and bringing us to a land full of all good, and corresponding to this He said ״קָּנֶךָ״. Third, that He fashioned us with a supreme and exalted fashioning by placing His Shekhinah among us and making us prophets, and this is a great fashioning — that He made us a vessel worthy to receive prophecy — and corresponding to this He said ״עָשְׂךָ״, meaning a new act beyond the creation alluded to in the expression ״אָבִיךָ״. Fourth, that He established us with an eternal establishment to merit through it the life of the World to Come, which is the essence. And the intention in all this is that a base man would not commit baseness against one possessing all these qualities unless on account of his being a fool, and this is what he said: ״נָבָל וְלֹא חָכָם״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {2 "The phrase כי הנבל יכיר שחושך מיושר אך למחסור is rendered hyper-literally; the argument appears to be that a base person knows that failing to act uprightly is attributable only to deficiency, yet wisdom would override this."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:11.149787247Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}